      <h2 id="status" class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Draw Status: The November 2026 Pause</h2>

      <p>
        If you are searching for the "last draw Express Entry" this month, the answer has not changed since October 28. IRCC announced on October 16, 2026 that new CRS rules would take effect on November 3, that profiles already in the pool would be rescored automatically, and that the recalculation "may take up to two weeks" with invitation rounds paused in the meantime. IRCC's Express Entry changes page says rounds will start again when the recalculation is complete. It gives no date.
      </p>
      <p>
        As of November 13, 2026, no round 454 appears in IRCC's rounds data. The two-week estimate runs to about November 17, but that is the outer edge of an estimate, not a scheduled draw. We don't predict draw dates here. When rounds resume, the first cutoffs will reflect the new grid, so expect them to differ from the October numbers in either direction.
      </p>

      <h2 id="types" class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Express Entry Round Types in 2026</h2>

      <p>IRCC runs three kinds of rounds:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
        <li><strong>General rounds</strong> are open to candidates in all Express Entry programs. There were none in 2026 up to October 28.</li>
        <li><strong>Program-specific rounds</strong> target one program. In 2026 these were Canadian Experience Class (CEC) rounds and Provincial Nominee Program (PNP) rounds for candidates who hold a provincial or territorial nomination.</li>
        <li><strong>Category-based rounds</strong> target candidates who meet a category the Minister has set to meet an economic goal.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">The 2026 categories</h3>
      <p>
        IRCC's category-based selection page lists ten categories: French-language proficiency; healthcare and social services occupations; STEM occupations; trade occupations; education occupations; transport occupations; physicians with Canadian work experience; senior managers with Canadian work experience; researchers with Canadian work experience; and skilled military recruits. IRCC announced the 2026 set in February 2026, adding researchers, senior managers, transport and skilled military recruits alongside the renewed categories.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most occupation categories require at least 12 months of full-time work experience (or the part-time equivalent) in one listed occupation within the past three years, gained in Canada or abroad. The physician, senior manager and researcher categories require that experience to be Canadian. The French category has no work experience rule but requires at least CLB 7 in all four French abilities. Check the occupation lists on IRCC's page before assuming you qualify; our guides to <a href="/articles/express-entry-transport-occupations-guide-2026" class="text-blue-600 underline">transport occupations</a> and <a href="/articles/express-entry-foreign-medical-doctors-guide-2026" class="text-blue-600 underline">foreign medical doctors</a> go deeper on two of them.
      </p>

